OpenPyCharm Frontend M0
Independent OpenPyCharm source under the repository LICENSE.

This default-off, fixture-only native API plugin is not included in the product
packaging pipeline and does not contain JetBrains proprietary JavaScript code.
It uses the authenticated open-source IntelliJ Platform SDK supplied separately.

Node 24.22.3, TypeScript Language Server 6.1.0 and TypeScript 6.0.3 are separately
authenticated in an owned development cache, never installed by opening a file.
The runtime retains original Node LICENSE/third-party text, TLS LICENSE,
TypeScript LICENSE/ThirdPartyNoticeText and full original legal files for the
21 exact npm packages embedded in the published TLS CLI bundle. Their original
archives, SRI/SHA/size, legal file hashes and payload closure are pinned in
tools.lock.json. No npm lifecycle/build/install scripts are executed.

Native compilation and standalone stdio protocol checks do not establish
native PC module/service activation, editor/UI behavior, Windows execution,
installed-product acceptance, or full PyCharm frontend parity.

Native lifecycle candidate uses the existing public PC261 LSP/process APIs.
The process reader preserves CRLF framing as required by the Apache-2.0 public
LspClientDescriptor contract at the pinned open-source commit:
https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community/blob/456919a9624bae72ac12efafc35d2b916cb0c5c5/platform/lsp/src/api/LspClientDescriptor.kt
No proprietary JavaScript/TypeScript PSI or Ultimate implementation is included.
